__pycache__
.venv
*.csv
# Fits are saved as json (see `LogisticWinProbability.save`), and a fit is
# output -- rerunnable from the plays it came from. A fit worth keeping goes
# somewhere versioned deliberately, not in here by accident.
*.json
# And `lucky_ones/releases` is that deliberate place: the fits `MODELS` serves,
# which ship inside the wheel. Tracked on purpose -- pinning the package by rev
# has to pin the model too. hatchling reads this file when it decides what goes
# in the build, so an ignored fit would also be a fit missing from the install.
!lucky_ones/releases/*.json
# And the validation reports under docs/, for the same reason: every figure in
# docs/epa-validation.md is read from one, so a claim about a model changing is
# a diff rather than a screenshot. `make validate` rewrites them.
!docs/validation-*.json
# A devcontainer config is hand-written input, not scratch output
!**/.devcontainer/*.json
.env

# Machine-local devcontainer settings -- the AWS_PROFILE to use, mainly. The
# point of the file is to keep that out of here; local.env.example is the
# tracked copy that documents it. (The `.env` rule above doesn't cover this
# one: an unanchored pattern matches a whole path component, not a suffix.)
.devcontainer/local.env

logs/
plays/
